---
import ShowcaseLayout from "../../layouts/ShowcaseLayout.astro";
import ShowcasePageHeader from "../../components/showcase/ShowcasePageHeader.astro";
import ShowcaseAnchorNav from "../../components/showcase/ShowcaseAnchorNav.astro";
import ShowcaseSection from "../../components/showcase/ShowcaseSection.astro";
import ShowcaseExample from "../../components/showcase/ShowcaseExample.astro";
import ShowcaseEmptyState from "../../components/showcase/ShowcaseEmptyState.astro";
import DetailModal from "../../components/interactions/display/DetailModal.astro";
import DefinitionList from "../../components/typography/DefinitionList.astro";
import QuoteBlock from "../../components/typography/QuoteBlock.astro";
import StatisticBlock from "../../components/typography/StatisticBlock.astro";
import TextLayout from "../../components/typography/TextLayout.astro";
import TypeText from "../../components/typography/TypeText.astro";
import { isShowcaseItemVisible } from "../../data/showcase-registry";

const approvedStack = `system-ui, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif`;
const typographyVisible = isShowcaseItemVisible("type-scale");
const typographyAnchors = [
  { label: "Hierarchy", href: "#type-hierarchy" },
  { label: "Display", href: "#display-statements" },
  { label: "Reading", href: "#reading-layouts" },
  { label: "Quotes", href: "#quotes-editorial" },
  { label: "Structured text", href: "#structured-text" },
  { label: "Values", href: "#statistics-values" },
  { label: "Emphasis", href: "#surfaces-emphasis" },
  { label: "Resilience", href: "#content-resilience" },
];
---

<ShowcaseLayout
  pageTitle="Typography | Quick Course Kit"
  description="Controlled typography and text-layout patterns for AI-generated Quick Courses."
  activeCategory="typography"
>
  <ShowcasePageHeader
    title="Typography"
    description="A controlled system for editorial learning content: semantic type roles, readable measures and responsive text layouts."
  />

  {typographyVisible && (
    <div class="mt-6">
      <ShowcaseAnchorNav label="Typography sections" items={typographyAnchors} />
    </div>
  )}

  <div class="showcase-section-stack mt-10">
    {!typographyVisible && <ShowcaseEmptyState />}

    {typographyVisible && (
      <ShowcaseSection id="typography-system" title="Typography and text layout system" description="Curated review specimens show the available system choices, not every possible permutation.">
        <ShowcaseExample id="type-scale" title="Quick Course Typography System" purpose="A semantic, system-font typography foundation for readable, responsive and AI-safe course content.">
          <div class="qc-type-showcase">
            <div class="qc-type-showcase__controls">
              <DetailModal
                id="typography-usage-guidance"
                triggerLabel="Typography usage guidance"
                triggerIcon="information"
                triggerVariant="secondary"
                heading="Typography usage guidance"
              >
                <div class="di-dialog__content">
                  <p>Choose type by instructional purpose first. Use a standard heading and body treatment when the content does not need special emphasis.</p>
                  <ul class="di-dialog__list">
                    <li>Use Display only for short opening statements, major transitions or memorable concepts. Long copy should use a normal heading.</li>
                    <li>Use a Lead for one concise introduction. Keep long-form reading left aligned in a narrow or standard measure.</li>
                    <li>Preserve the HTML heading hierarchy. Visual size is independent from semantic heading level.</li>
                    <li>Use two or three columns only for short related content. Put detailed explanations in one readable column.</li>
                    <li>Use quotes for genuine quotations or clearly marked internal examples. Pull quotes are non-essential emphasis, never required reading.</li>
                    <li>Use serif, monospace and cursive accents sparingly. Cursive is a review-only option for one short, non-essential phrase.</li>
                    <li>Use the course theme and explicit visual direction before selecting a surface or accent tone. Do not add an eyebrow to every heading.</li>
                  </ul>
                </div>
              </DetailModal>

              <DetailModal
                id="typography-technical-implementation"
                triggerLabel="Typography technical implementation"
                triggerIcon="settings"
                triggerVariant="secondary"
                heading="Typography technical implementation"
              >
                <div class="di-dialog__content">
                  <p>The system uses no external fonts. It maps semantic roles, measures, families, weights, tones, surfaces and layouts to a controlled CSS variable layer.</p>
                  <ul class="di-dialog__list">
                    <li>Default content uses the approved native system sans stack. Serif, monospace and generic cursive are controlled local fallbacks.</li>
                    <li>Responsive roles use clamp-based scales, readable line heights and controlled measures rather than raw author-supplied pixels.</li>
                    <li>Text layouts use semantic grid patterns that collapse in DOM reading order. Quotes, lists, definitions and values retain native HTML semantics.</li>
                    <li>Future theme tokens can map font, colour, surface and spacing values without changing content structure. The system stays static-site and SCORM compatible.</li>
                  </ul>
                </div>
              </DetailModal>
            </div>

            <section id="type-hierarchy" class="qc-type-showcase__section scroll-mt-28" aria-labelledby="type-hierarchy-heading">
              <h4 id="type-hierarchy-heading">Type hierarchy</h4>
              <p class="qc-type-showcase__intro">Semantic heading level and visual role stay separate, so a course can preserve its outline while choosing a controlled editorial treatment.</p>
              <div class="qc-type-hierarchy">
                <div class="qc-type-hierarchy__item"><span>Display XL</span><TypeText as="p" role="display-xl" weight="bold">Make every conversation count.</TypeText></div>
                <div class="qc-type-hierarchy__item"><span>Display Large</span><TypeText as="p" role="display-lg" weight="semibold">The first question changes everything.</TypeText></div>
                <div class="qc-type-hierarchy__item"><span>Display Medium</span><TypeText as="p" role="display-md" family="serif" italic>Listen before you solve.</TypeText></div>
                <div class="qc-type-hierarchy__item"><span>H1 visual role</span><TypeText as="p" role="heading-xl" weight="bold">A clearer product conversation starts here</TypeText></div>
                <div class="qc-type-hierarchy__item"><span>H2 visual role</span><TypeText as="p" role="heading-lg" weight="semibold">Guide the decision, not just the transaction</TypeText></div>
                <div class="qc-type-hierarchy__item"><span>H3 visual role</span><TypeText as="p" role="heading-md" weight="semibold">Keep the key comparison visible</TypeText></div>
                <div class="qc-type-hierarchy__item"><span>H4 visual role</span><TypeText as="p" role="heading-sm" weight="semibold">Name the next action and its timing</TypeText></div>
                <div class="qc-type-hierarchy__item"><span>Label</span><TypeText as="p" role="eyebrow" weight="semibold">PRODUCT KNOWLEDGE</TypeText></div>
                <div class="qc-type-hierarchy__item"><span>Lead</span><TypeText as="p" role="lead">Use a short lead to bridge a major heading and the explanation that follows.</TypeText></div>
                <div class="qc-type-hierarchy__item"><span>Caption</span><TypeText as="p" role="caption" tone="muted">Illustrative specimen for Quick Course review only.</TypeText></div>
              </div>
            </section>

            <section id="display-statements" class="qc-type-showcase__section scroll-mt-28" aria-labelledby="display-statements-heading">
              <h4 id="display-statements-heading">Display and statement typography</h4>
              <div class="qc-type-display-grid qc-type-display-grid--three">
                <TextLayout layout="statement" surface="light" spacing="spacious">
                  <TypeText as="p" role="display-lg" align="center" weight="light">LISTEN<br />BEFORE YOU SOLVE</TypeText>
                </TextLayout>
                <TextLayout layout="statement" surface="primary" spacing="spacious">
                  <TypeText as="p" role="statement" align="center" weight="bold" tone="inverse">SMALL ACTIONS.<br />BIG IMPACT.</TypeText>
                </TextLayout>
                <TextLayout layout="statement" surface="none" spacing="spacious">
                  <TypeText as="p" role="display-md" family="serif" align="center" italic>The product story should make the choice feel simpler.</TypeText>
                  <p class="qc-type-cursive-note">A quick human reminder</p>
                </TextLayout>
              </div>
            </section>

            <section id="headings-introductions" class="qc-type-showcase__section scroll-mt-28" aria-labelledby="headings-introductions-heading">
              <h4 id="headings-introductions-heading">Headings and introductions</h4>
              <TextLayout layout="split" surface="none" spacing="spacious">
                <div>
                  <TypeText as="p" role="eyebrow" weight="semibold">BEFORE YOU BEGIN</TypeText>
                  <TypeText as="h5" role="heading-xl" weight="bold">A well-timed pause can make a policy explanation easier to trust.</TypeText>
                </div>
                <div class="qc-text-layout__prose">
                  <TypeText as="p" role="lead">Use a clear opening to name what matters, then help the learner connect that point to a practical action.</TypeText>
                  <TypeText as="p" role="body" tone="muted">This split layout keeps the heading and supporting explanation visually related while preserving the logical reading order.</TypeText>
                </div>
              </TextLayout>
              <TextLayout layout="statement" surface="secondary" spacing="spacious">
                <TypeText as="h5" role="heading-lg" align="center" weight="semibold">A centred heading is for short, high-impact transitions.</TypeText>
                <TypeText as="p" role="lead" align="center">Keep the supporting line brief enough to remain easy to scan.</TypeText>
              </TextLayout>
            </section>

            <section id="reading-layouts" class="qc-type-showcase__section scroll-mt-28" aria-labelledby="reading-layouts-heading">
              <h4 id="reading-layouts-heading">Reading layouts</h4>
              <TextLayout layout="reading-narrow" surface="none" spacing="standard">
                <TypeText as="h5" role="heading-md" weight="semibold">Narrow reading column</TypeText>
                <div class="qc-text-layout__prose">
                  <TypeText as="p" role="body">When a policy changes, the learner needs the reason, the practical effect and the next step in that order. A focused reading measure makes the explanation feel manageable instead of dense.</TypeText>
                  <TypeText as="p" role="body">Use this pattern for reflective learning, detailed guidance and any content that needs more than a short scan.</TypeText>
                </div>
              </TextLayout>

              <TextLayout layout="two-equal" surface="muted" spacing="standard">
                <div class="qc-text-layout__prose">
                  <TypeText as="h5" role="heading-sm" weight="semibold">Explain the feature</TypeText>
                  <TypeText as="p" role="body">Name the benefit in plain language, then connect it to the customer need that makes it relevant.</TypeText>
                </div>
                <div class="qc-text-layout__prose">
                  <TypeText as="h5" role="heading-sm" weight="semibold">Confirm the outcome</TypeText>
                  <TypeText as="p" role="body">Close with the action, timing and a simple way to check progress later.</TypeText>
                </div>
              </TextLayout>

              <TextLayout layout="two-main" surface="none" spacing="standard">
                <div class="qc-text-layout__prose">
                  <TypeText as="h5" role="heading-md" weight="semibold">Main explanation with a supporting aside</TypeText>
                  <TypeText as="p" role="body">A stock-handling guide may need room for its main process while keeping a smaller reminder close by. The larger column carries the instructional sequence; the aside reinforces the one detail that prevents an avoidable error.</TypeText>
                </div>
                <aside class="qc-text-layout__aside"><QuoteBlock quote="Keep the product label visible until the final check is complete." variant="pull" /></aside>
              </TextLayout>

              <TextLayout layout="three" surface="none" spacing="standard">
                <div><TypeText as="h5" role="heading-sm" weight="semibold">Notice</TypeText><TypeText as="p" role="body-compact">Observe the signal before making an assumption.</TypeText></div>
                <div><TypeText as="h5" role="heading-sm" weight="semibold">Clarify</TypeText><TypeText as="p" role="body-compact">Ask the one question that changes the next step.</TypeText></div>
                <div><TypeText as="h5" role="heading-sm" weight="semibold">Confirm</TypeText><TypeText as="p" role="body-compact">Restate the agreed action and timing.</TypeText></div>
              </TextLayout>
            </section>

            <section id="quotes-editorial" class="qc-type-showcase__section scroll-mt-28" aria-labelledby="quotes-editorial-heading">
              <h4 id="quotes-editorial-heading">Quotes and editorial emphasis</h4>
              <div class="qc-quote-grid">
                <QuoteBlock quote="Clarity is not saying more. It is helping someone understand what matters." citation="Internal learning example" variant="rule" />
                <QuoteBlock quote="The best recommendation starts with the question you ask before you speak." citation="Unattributed training prompt" variant="center" />
                <QuoteBlock quote="A useful explanation makes the next action feel possible." citation="Illustrative quote" variant="surface" />
                <TextLayout layout="pull-quote" surface="none" spacing="standard">
                  <div class="qc-text-layout__prose"><TypeText as="p" role="body">A leadership update can include the practical context first, then use a pull quote to reinforce a memorable idea without interrupting the reading flow.</TypeText></div>
                  <aside class="qc-text-layout__aside"><QuoteBlock quote="Say what changes, why it matters and where support is available." variant="pull" /></aside>
                </TextLayout>
              </div>
            </section>

            <section id="structured-text" class="qc-type-showcase__section scroll-mt-28" aria-labelledby="structured-text-heading">
              <h4 id="structured-text-heading">Structured text</h4>
              <div class="qc-structured-grid qc-structured-grid--three">
                <div>
                  <TypeText as="h5" role="heading-sm" weight="semibold">Checklist</TypeText>
                  <ul class="qc-checklist">
                    <li>Check the product name and size.</li>
                    <li>Confirm the customer’s intended use.</li>
                    <li>State the next action clearly.</li>
                  </ul>
                </div>
                <div>
                  <TypeText as="h5" role="heading-sm" weight="semibold">Large numbered steps</TypeText>
                  <ol class="qc-numbered-steps">
                    <li><div><h5>Prepare</h5><p>Have the relevant information ready before the conversation starts.</p></div></li>
                    <li><div><h5>Guide</h5><p>Connect one useful feature to the learner or customer need.</p></div></li>
                    <li><div><h5>Confirm</h5><p>Name the action, owner and realistic timing.</p></div></li>
                  </ol>
                </div>
                <div>
                  <TypeText as="h5" role="heading-sm" weight="semibold">Question and answer</TypeText>
                  <div class="qc-question-answer">
                    <p class="qc-question-answer__question">What should you confirm first?</p>
                    <p class="qc-question-answer__answer">Start by clarifying how the person intends to use the product or process.</p>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>

              <DefinitionList
                variant="split"
                items={[
                  { term: "Lead", definition: "A concise opening paragraph that introduces the main idea before normal body copy." },
                  { term: "Statement", definition: "A short high-impact phrase for a transition, reminder or key learning moment." },
                  { term: "Caption", definition: "Small supporting context for an image, figure, value or illustrative specimen." },
                ]}
              />

              <div class="qc-do-dont">
                <section><TypeText as="h5" role="heading-sm" weight="semibold">Do</TypeText><ul><li>Use one readable column for detailed policy explanation.</li><li>Use a short label only when it adds context.</li></ul></section>
                <section><TypeText as="h5" role="heading-sm" weight="semibold">Do not</TypeText><ul><li>Put two long articles side by side.</li><li>Use a quote style for essential instructions.</li></ul></section>
              </div>
            </section>

            <section id="statistics-values" class="qc-type-showcase__section scroll-mt-28" aria-labelledby="statistics-values-heading">
              <h4 id="statistics-values-heading">Statistics and key values</h4>
              <p class="qc-type-showcase__intro">All values below are illustrative Showcase content, not business reporting.</p>
              <div class="qc-stat-grid qc-stat-grid--three">
                <StatisticBlock value="30" label="Days in an illustrative return window" detail="Example only" />
                <StatisticBlock value="3" label="Steps in a product conversation" detail="Ask. Listen. Recommend." align="center" />
                <StatisticBlock value="98%" label="Illustrative completion example" detail="Not live course data" surface="primary" align="center" />
              </div>
              <TextLayout layout="two-aside" surface="light" spacing="standard">
                <StatisticBlock value="2:1" label="Controlled column ratio" detail="A main explanation can sit beside a concise supporting aside." />
                <div class="qc-text-layout__prose"><TypeText as="h5" role="heading-md" weight="semibold">A value should support the learning point.</TypeText><TypeText as="p" role="body">Use a statistic only when it gives useful context. Avoid presenting illustrative Showcase values as factual business claims.</TypeText></div>
              </TextLayout>
            </section>

            <section id="surfaces-emphasis" class="qc-type-showcase__section scroll-mt-28" aria-labelledby="surfaces-emphasis-heading">
              <h4 id="surfaces-emphasis-heading">Surfaces, colour and inline emphasis</h4>
              <div class="qc-type-specimen-grid">
                <TextLayout layout="band" surface="dark" spacing="spacious">
                  <TypeText as="p" role="statement" tone="inverse" weight="bold">START WITH THE NEED.</TypeText>
                  <TypeText as="p" role="body" tone="muted">Inverse text remains controlled and readable on a dark semantic surface.</TypeText>
                </TextLayout>
                <TextLayout layout="band" surface="accent" spacing="spacious">
                  <TypeText as="p" role="heading-lg" weight="semibold">A muted surface can still carry a clear instruction.</TypeText>
                  <TypeText as="p" role="body">Surface treatment supports hierarchy; it does not create a different content component.</TypeText>
                </TextLayout>
              </div>
              <p class="qc-inline-demo">Use <strong>strong emphasis</strong> for an important phrase, <em>italic styling</em> for a short editorial shift, an <a href="#reading-layouts">explicit link label</a> for navigation, <mark>highlight only what matters</mark>, <code>course-progress-state</code> for a system value, <kbd>Enter</kbd> for a keyboard command, <abbr title="Standard operating procedure">SOP</abbr> for an abbreviation, H<sub>2</sub>O for subscript and 10<sup>th</sup> for superscript.</p>
              <div class="qc-type-weight-row" aria-label="Approved type weight specimen">
                <span class="qc-type--weight-light">Light display</span><span class="qc-type--weight-regular">Regular</span><span class="qc-type--weight-medium">Medium</span><span class="qc-type--weight-semibold">Semibold</span><span class="qc-type--weight-bold">Bold</span><span class="qc-type--weight-heavy">Heavy</span>
              </div>
            </section>

            <section id="same-content" class="qc-type-showcase__section scroll-mt-28" aria-labelledby="same-content-heading">
              <h4 id="same-content-heading">Same content, different treatment</h4>
              <p class="qc-type-showcase__intro">Each specimen uses the identical content so reviewers can compare typography rather than copy.</p>
              <div class="qc-same-content-grid qc-same-content-grid--three">
                <div><TypeText as="p" role="heading-md" weight="semibold">Listening is an active skill.</TypeText><TypeText as="p" role="body">Listening is an active skill.</TypeText></div>
                <TextLayout layout="statement" surface="none" spacing="compact"><TypeText as="p" role="statement" align="center" family="serif" italic>Listening is an active skill.</TypeText></TextLayout>
                <TextLayout layout="statement" surface="dark" spacing="compact"><TypeText as="p" role="heading-md" align="center" tone="inverse" weight="semibold">Listening is an active skill.</TypeText></TextLayout>
              </div>
            </section>

            <section id="content-resilience" class="qc-type-showcase__section scroll-mt-28" aria-labelledby="content-resilience-heading">
              <h4 id="content-resilience-heading">Content resilience</h4>
              <div class="qc-type-resilience">
                <TypeText as="p" role="heading-xl" weight="bold">How do you explain a complex operational change without overwhelming someone who needs to use it before their next shift?</TypeText>
                <div class="qc-type-prose">
                  <p>Long form content stays in a readable measure, remains left aligned and uses ordinary wrapping. It does not shrink or truncate merely to fit a decorative treatment.</p>
                  <p><a href="#type-hierarchy">Review the controlled heading hierarchy and reading-width guidance for long course content</a>.</p>
                  <p class="qc-type-resilience__identifier"><code>policyAcknowledgementAndExceptionHandlingReferenceIdentifier</code></p>
                </div>
              </div>
            </section>
          </div>
        </ShowcaseExample>
      </ShowcaseSection>
    )}
  </div>
</ShowcaseLayout>
